<p>This is a real tragedy, because the five other parts of the drawing are actually there in GPT-4’s output. However, it used the background() function for the background colour of each segment, accidently filling the entire canvas and covering the earlier segments.</p><p>Additionally, GPT-4 chose function names that are already in use by p5js, such as circle() and rect(). </p><p>I fixed these bits, so we can take a look at how it did otherwise. It hasn’t quite been able to follow the sentence structure of the instructions, but it’s another clear leap forward from GPT-3. </p>


